    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear anchor for the lineup; his score of 87.42 is fueled by an elite 0.474 xwOBA and a generous matchup against Grayson Rodriguez, who carries a shaky 5.28 xERA. Following close behind, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.53) and **Trea Turner** (66.99) are priority starts. Both players offer significant stolen base upside against relatively slow deliveries, which is essential given our roster's prioritization of speed. **Caleb Durbin** also grades out as a top-tier option (72.37) because his matchup against Jacob Lopez exploits a favorable park factor and a weak 5.54 xERA, maximizing his potential to contribute across our five categories.\n\nPlatoon advantages and lineup position are the primary drivers for today's configuration. We are leaning heavily into **Dillon Dingler** (63.75) and **Christian Yelich** (63.16), both of whom benefit from dynamic platoon advantages that inflate their daily efficiency. Conversely, we must monitor the status of **Carson Benge**; while his score of 57.57 is respectable, the 45% rain risk creates a volatility threshold that warrants keeping a close eye on pre-game reports. **Junior Caminero** remains in the lineup despite a sub-60 score (57.41) due to his positional necessity, though he faces a tougher challenge against the high-skill arm of MacKenzie Gore.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was excluding **Pedro Ramirez**, who fell just short with a 39.68 rating. While he offers some utility, his projected batting position at the bottom of the order and the lack of a strong platoon edge led the optimizer to prioritize the higher-ceiling outcomes of **Josh Smith** and **Nelson Velazquez**. With **Hyeseong Kim** currently assigned to the Oklahoma City Comets and **Kyle Schwarber** unavailable, the bench depth is strictly limited today. We will rely on our starters to overcome the defensive hurdle of facing Logan Webb with both **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich** in the mix, hoping that high-volume contact mitigates the difficulty of the matchup.",
